    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="f49f969d-f703-545f-a45d-f7bde7becec2" activityNameId="5257f98e-cd39-56f8-9f0f-b94911e70e2f" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, fluorescent lamps</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, fluorescent lamps
The multioutput-process "treatment fluorescent lamps" delivers the co-products " disposal, fluorescent lamps”, "mercury, from fluorescent lamps treatment, at plant", "glass cullet, from fluorescent lamps treatment, at plant ",”rare-earth activated phosphors, from fluorescent lamps treatment, at plant” and "secondary metals, from fluorescent lamps treatment, at plant". The allocation is done 100% to the disposal process.;
UUID: 65639582-0c12-4215-bf83-7a1b3de529de
This dataset represents the treatment of fluorescent lamps. It includes infrastructure, energy consumption, waste and air emissions and an estimation of the efforts for transportation. The process has no water consumption and no water emissions.
Location: Information from German recycling companies - used as global average data.
Technology: Dry dismantling technology of fluorescent lamps – with cutting, blowing, crushing and air exhaust cleaning steps.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: 120 kt fluorescent lamp annually sold
Sampling: Company information &amp; own estimation 
Extrapolations: Data from CRT glass treatment and from general shredding activities used when no proper information available.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_65639582-0c12-4215-bf83-7a1b3de529de.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
